course: dictionary
lesson: 4839
title: Fire hydrant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be hard to picture, but the words around it often explain it. Read this: «You never play with a fire hydrant, because it is for firefighters; opening one for fun wastes water and can leave firefighters without enough water pressure to fight a fire.»
explain: The clues are firefighters, fight a fire and water. So a fire hydrant must be a place where firefighters get water to put out fires. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "You never play with a place where firefighters get water, because it is for firefighters" still makes sense.
explain: The sentence also tells you what to do. Hydrants are for firefighters, so you must leave them alone. Opening one for fun is wasteful and dangerous, because there might not be enough water when a real fire needs it.
fact: A hydrant is a pipe in the street that firefighters use to get water.
fact: Fire hydrants are often short red or yellow posts.
fact: In the UK, hydrants are often under small metal covers in the pavement, marked with a yellow «H» sign.
fact: Cars must never park in front of a hydrant, so that firefighters can reach the water quickly.
fact: «Wastes» means uses up for nothing, so opening a hydrant for fun wastes water.
exercise: «You never play with a fire hydrant, because it is for firefighters.» Who is a hydrant for? | *Firefighters | Shopkeepers | Children playing | Dog walkers
exercise: «Opening one for fun wastes water.» What does wastes mean here? | Saves | Cleans | Freezes | *Uses up for nothing
exercise: In the UK, a yellow «H» sign in the pavement shows what? | A shop | A hospital | A bus stop | *A fire hydrant is under the metal cover
test: Why should children never open a fire hydrant? | It is too heavy to lift | It is only for sweeping the street | *It wastes water, and firefighters may not have enough when there is a fire | It makes the pavement wet for skating
test: Which choice shows safe behaviour near a hydrant? | *Keep the area clear so firefighters can reach it | Climb on top of it to look at the street | Open it on a hot day to cool down | Park in front of it to save space
exam: What is a fire hydrant? | A sort of shop sign | A red school bag | *A pipe in the street where firefighters connect hoses to get water | A tall tree in the park
